t\",\n          \"value\": \"The user initially found community event planning exciting but became overwhelmed and disheartened by the complexities of organizing a book swap, including coordinating genres, schedules, and fair distribution. They later had a positive experience organizing a successful author interview event that generated community excitement, making the effort feel worthwhile. They also joined a reading marathon for charity, which provided a strong sense of community and shared purpose. However, they had two negative experiences with a community buying group, finding it less engaging and stagnant due to lack of dynamic interactions and clear direction. Overall, the user has experienced both rewarding and disappointing community involvement, with the positive events being well-organized and fostering connection, while the negative ones lacked engagement and structure.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s21\", \"s13\", \"s5\", \"s20\", \"s32\", \"s12\", \"s47\", \"s22\", \"s48\", \"s30\", \"s31\", \"s4\", \"s3\", \"s49\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"lifetime\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user describes multiple past community involvement experiences. The book swap planning (s3-s5) became overwhelming and disheartening. The author interview event (s12-s13) was exciting and rewarding. The reading marathon (s30-s32) provided a strong sense of community. The buying group experiences (s20-s22, s47-s49) were disappointing due to lack of engagement and direction. These are all relevant past changes in attitudes and circumstances.\",\n          \"summary_revision\": {\n            \"supersedes_route_ids\": [\"fact_5c114d5ee39cc1f868be58a6\"],\n            \"previous_version\": 1,\n            \"reason\": \"This revision incorporates the same sourced historical facts as the previous summary, re-expressed with consistent scope and citations. No new eviden