and the current version.\nsummary_revision_contracts.required_source_ids covers replacing ALL offered\neligible_route_ids. When selecting only a subset, retain those selected routes'\nsources, their actual-parent source closure and relevant same-variable counters.\nStructured repair feedback gives the exact required set for that draft's targets.\nThis capability is optional, not a requirement to revise an unchanged summary.\nWith no new observation, return observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts and all terminal/audit variables\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\nThe four public_options correspond in list order to (a), (b), (c), (d). They are candidate answers, not evidence. Put the selected label only in final_prediction; keep the entire response as the required JSON object with all other fields required by its schema. Never return a bare label.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"audit_verdict\":{\"enum\":[\"supported\",\"unknown\",\"conflict\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"final_prediction\":{\"enum\":[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\",null],\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"semantic_answer\":{},\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"lifetime\"}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_e6ff3737a45feca785fd5199\",\"fact_92f951b99fe6091e9310ecb2\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"user_interests\"}}}],\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"allOf\":[{\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"contradiction\"}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"minItems\":1}}}}],\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent_versions\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"object\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"source_ids\":{\"description\":\"Exact visible source_spans[].id aliases, such as s3; never document IDs or invented IDs.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"time_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"value\":{}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"stance\",\"value\",\"source_ids\",\"entity_scope\",\"time_scope\",\"parent_versions\",\"retract_ids\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"unresolved\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"variable\":{\"enum\":[\"user_interests\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"variable\",\"observations\",\"unresolved\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":1,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"}},\"required\":[\"slots\"],\"type\":\"object\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"original_question\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\",\"output_slot\":\"response\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[\"event_experience\",\"user_interests\",\"constraints\",\"changes\"],\"execution\":\"compose\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\\nEstablished event_experience: The user has had mixed recent experiences with community event planning. They found planning a book swap overwhelming and disheartening due to logistical complexities, but successfully conducted an engaging author interview event that felt rewarding. They also joined a reading marathon for charity that fostered a strong sense of community, and started a regular volunteering schedule at a local library that they find fulfilling. However, they were disappointed by a community buying group that lacked engagement and clear direction.\\nEstablished user_interests: The user has a strong and enduring interest in community involvement, particularly through literature and reading-related activities. They have organized a book swap (though found it overwhelming), participated in a reading marathon for charity (positive experience), conducted an interview with a well-known author leading to a community event (positive experience), started regular volunteering at a local library (positive experience), curated a list of must-read books for a community newsletter (positive experience), helped organize book recommendations for library patrons (positive experience), joined a local book club focused on contemporary fiction (positive experience), attended a national literature festival (positive experience), and formed a partnership with local artists to create book-themed merchandise for events (positive experience). They also joined a community buying group but found it less engaging. Their values include fostering literacy, community connection, and shared experiences around books.\\nEstablished constraints: The user faced significant stress and overwhelm while planning a community book swap, due to the complexities of coordinating genres, managing schedules, ensuring enough participants, and devising a fair distribution system. This led to disheartenment about pursuing similar events. Additionally, the user found a community buying group less engaging than expected, with stagnant conversations and a lack of clear focus or direction, leading to disappointment. These challenges could affect continuing community event planning.\\nEstablished changes: The user initially found community event planning exciting but became overwhelmed and disheartened by the complexities of organizing a book swap, including coordinating genres, schedules, and fair distribution. They later had a positive experience organizing a successful author interview event that generated community excitement, making the effort feel worthwhile. They also joined a reading marathon for charity, which provided a strong sense of community and shared purpose. However, they had two negative experiences with a community buying group, finding it less engaging and stagnant due to lack of dynamic interactions and clear direction. Overall, the user has experienced both rewarding and disappointing community involvement, with the positive events being well-organized and fostering connection, while the negative ones lacked engagement and structure.\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"deb8c244225e471f3862a2ad84efa6a8b86c3ff5cfd9fca5a3bae4f5370d7ad8\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"4ae75ff431f54f7c73cbe3a0e3a8fba87e7b7c6f4f42c747d4b48a5ee47b9c56\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"0c279655aa3e6532d7c207ec52fa91cf587c7fedc01351de965cc12941912b25\"},\"variables\":{\"user_interests\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"user_interests\",\"open\":true,\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"user_interests\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"user_interests\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{\"event_experience\":{\"value\":\"The user has had mixed recent experiences with community event planning. They found planning a book swap overwhelming and disheartening due to logistical complexities, but successfully conducted an engaging author interview event that felt rewarding. They also joined a r