eturn observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts and all terminal/audit variables\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\nThe four public_options correspond in list order to (a), (b), (c), (d). They are candidate answers, not evidence. Put the selected label only in final_prediction; keep the entire response as the required JSON object with all other fields required by its schema. Never return a bare label.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"audit_verdict\":{\"enum\":[\"supported\",\"unknown\",\"conflict\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"final_prediction\":{\"enum\":[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\",null],\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"semantic_answer\":{},\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"lifetime\"}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_e6ff3737a45feca785fd5199\",\"fact_92f951b99fe6091e9310ecb2\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"user_interests\"}}}],\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"allOf\":[{\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"contradiction\"}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"minItems\":1}}}}],\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent_versions\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"object\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"source_ids\":{\"description\":\"Exact visible source_spans[].id aliases, such as s3; never document IDs or invented IDs.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"time_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"value\":{}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"stance\",\"value\",\"source_ids\",\"entity_scope\",\"time_scope\",\"parent_versions\",\"retract_ids\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"unresolved\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"variable\":{\"enum\":[\"user_interests\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"variable\",\"observations\",\"unresolved\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":1,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"}},\"required\":[\"slots\",\"audit_verdict\"],\"type\":\"object\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"original_question\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\",\"output_slot\":\"response\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[\"event_experience\",\"user_interests\",\"constraints\",\"changes\"],\"execution\":\"compose\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"9662d4bf623fa889da36b97eabb5a3cdd00b432c1b2b232f12c90bbc109b61c3\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"4ae75ff431f54f7c73cbe3a0e3a8fba87e7b7c6f4f42c747d4b48a5ee47b9c56\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"0c279655aa3e6532d7c207ec52fa91cf587c7fedc01351de965cc12941912b25\"},\"variables\":{\"user_interests\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"user_interests\",\"open\":true,\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"user_interests\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"user_interests\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{\"event_experience\":{\"value\":\"The user has had mixed recent experiences with community event planning. They found planning a book swap overwhelming and disheartening due to logistical complexities, but successfully conducted an engaging author interview event that felt rewarding. They also joined a reading marathon for charity that fostered a strong sense of community, and started a regular volunteering schedule at a local library that they find fulfilling. However, they were disappointed by a community buying group that lacked engagement and clear direction.\",\"version\":1,\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"demand\":\"event_experience\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"recent\"}},\"user_interests\":{\"value\":\"The user has a strong and enduring interest in community involvement, particularly through literature and reading-related activities. They have organized a book swap (though found it overwhelming), participated in a reading marathon for charity (positive experience), conducted an interview with a well-known author leading to a community event (positive experience), started regular volunteering at a local library (positive experience), curated a list of must-read books for a community newsletter (positive experience), helped organize book recommendations for library patrons (positive experience), joined a local book club focused on contemporary fiction (positive experience), attended a national literature festival (positive experience), and formed a partnership with local artists to create book-themed merchandise for events (positive experience). They also joined a community buying group but found it less engaging. Their values include fostering literacy, community connection, and shared experiences around books.\",\"version\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"s78\",\"s40\",\"s105\",\"s121\",\"s104\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s79\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s58\",\"s113\",\"s95\",\"s77\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s57\",\"s31\",\"s120\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s112\",\"s49\",\"s96\"],\"demand\":\"user_interests\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\"}},\"constraints\":{\"value\":\"The user faced significant stress and overwhelm while planning a community book swap, due to the complexities of coordinating genres, managing schedules, ensuring enough participants, and devising a fair distribution system. This led to disheartenment about pursuing similar events. Additionally, the user found a community buying group less engaging than expected, with stagnant conversations and a lack of clear focus or direction, leading to disappointment. These challenges could affect continuing community event planning.\",\"version\":1,\"source_ids\":[\"s21\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"demand\":\"constraints\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"recent\"}},\"changes\":{\"value\":\"The user initially found community event planning exciting but became overwhelmed and disheartened by the complexities of organizing a book swap, including coordinating genres, schedules, and fair distribution. They later had a positive experience organizing a successful author interview event that generated community excitement, making the effort feel worthwhile. They also joined a reading marathon for charity, which provided a strong sense of community and shared purpose. However, they had two negative experiences with a community buying group, finding it less engaging and stagnant due to lack of dynamic interactions and clear direction. Overall, the user has experienced both rewarding and disappointing community involvement, with the positive events being well-organized and fostering connection, while the negative ones lacked engagement and structure.\",\"version\":1,\"source_ids\":[\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"demand\":\"changes\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\"}}},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_e6ff3737a45feca785fd5199\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user has a strong interest in community involvement, particularly through literature and reading-related events. They have organized a book swap (though found it overwhelming), participated in a reading marathon for charity (positive experience), conducted an interview with a well-known author leading to a community event (positive experience), and started regular volunteering at a local library (positive experience). They also joined a community buying group but found it less engaging. Their values include fostering literacy, community connection, and shared experiences around books.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes multiple community activities: organizing a book swap (s3-s5), a reading marathon for charity (s30-s32), an author interview event (s12-s13), library volunteering (s39-s40), and a buying group (s20-s22, s47-s49). The positive experiences center on literature and community, while the buying group was disappointing. This supports a general interest in community involvement through literary and reading-related activities.\",\"variable\":\"user_interests\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"superseded_by\":[\"fact_92f951b99fe6091e9310ecb2\"]},{\"id\":\"fact_92f951b99fe6091e9310ecb2\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user has a strong and enduring interest in community involvement, particularly through literature and reading-related activities. They have organized a book swap (though found it overwhelming), participated in a reading marathon for charity (positive experience), conducted an interview with a well-known author leading to a community event (positive experience), started regular volunteering at a local library (positive experience), curated a list of must-read books for a community newsletter (positive experience), helped organize book recommendations for library patrons (positive experience), joined a local book club focused on contemporary fiction (positive experience), attended a national literature festival (positive experience), and formed a partnership with local artists to create book-themed merchandise for events (positive experience). They also joined a community buying group but found it less engaging. Their values include fostering literacy, community connection, and shared experiences around books.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s78\",\"s40\",\"s105\",\"s121\",\"s104\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s79\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s58\",\"s113\",\"s95\",\"s77\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s57\",\"s31\",\"s120\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s112\",\"s49\",\"s96\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes multiple community activities across various conversations: organizing a book swap (s3-s5), a reading marathon for charity (s30-s32), an author interview event (s12-s13), library volunteering (s39-s40), curating a book list for a newsletter (s57-s58), helping organize book recommendations at a library (s77-s79), joining a book club (s95-s96), attending a literature festival (s120-s121), and partnering with artists for book-themed merchandise (s104-s105). The buying group was disappointing (s20-s22, s47-s49). The positive experiences center on literature and community, supporting a general interest in community involvement through literary and reading-related activities.\",\"summary_revision\":{\"supersedes_route_ids\":[\"fact_e6ff3737a45feca785fd5199\"],\"previous_version\":1,\"reason\":\"Incorporating additional compatible evidence from new source spans (s57-s58, s77-s79, s95-s96, s104-s105, s112-s113, s120-s121) that further support the user's interest in community involvement through literature, while retaining all original evidence and the negative experience with the buying group.\"},\"variable\":\"user_interests\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,458,\"User: Organizing the book swap seemed like a delightful idea initially, but as I delved into the planning stage, the complexities started to unfold in ways I hadn't anticipated. The thoughts of coordinating different genres, managing people's varying schedules, and ensuring there were enough participants to make it worthwhile all became overwhelming. \",\"user\",[42]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",458,800,\"I found myself trying to devise a system that would work for everyone involved, but with each attempt, I felt more and more stressed rather than excited. The logistics of gathering different books, sorting them by category, and then figuring out how to distribute them fairly seemed like a task that was becoming more daunting by the minute. \",\"user\",[42]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",800,1014,\"Ultimately, it seemed that I was investing too much time and energy into something that was supposed to be a fun community experience, which left me feeling disheartened about pursuing similar events in the future.\",\"user\",[42]],[\"s12\",\"d2\",105,457,\"User: Lastly, I successfully conducted an engaging interview with a well-known author, which led to an exciting community event. The experience of speaking with someone who has had such a profound impact on the literary world was awe-inspiring. I learned so much not only about their writing process but also about their personal journey as an author. \",\"user\",[67]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",457,640,\"It felt like stepping into a world that was both familiar and completely new. Seeing the immediate excitement it generated in the community really made all the preparation worthwhile.\",\"user\",[67]],[\"s20\",\"d3\",107,359,\"User: Lastly, I joined a community-based buying group, but I found it less engaging than I anticipated. Initially, I was excited about the idea of being part of a collective, where people share and collaborate on purchases to benefit from bulk buying. \",\"user\",[138]],[\"s21\",\"d3\",359,728,\"I imagined engaging discussions with like-minded individuals about our shared interests and needs, perhaps even discovering new products or services I had never considered before. However, as time went on, I noticed that the interactions weren't as dynamic or fulfilling as I had hoped; there wasn't much enthusiasm in the conversations, and it felt somewhat stagnant. \",\"user\",[138]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",728,874,\"Additionally, I realized that the group didn't have a clear focus or direction, which contributed to my sense of disengagement and disappointment.\",\"user\",[138]],[\"s30\",\"d4\",105,450,\"User: I even joined a reading marathon for charity! It was a structured event that promoted community involvement, where participants from diverse backgrounds came together to share their love for reading. The organization of the event was meticulous, with schedules, reading lists, and even group discussions planned to enhance our experience. \",\"user\",[63]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",450,761,\"I witnessed how everyone was not just focused on individual achievements, but also on encouraging one another and celebrating our collective progress. It was refreshing to see people's eyes light up when they talked about their favorite books, creating bonds that seemed to transcend the pages we were turning. \",\"user\",[63]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",761,910,\"Ultimately, I found a real sense of community in the challenge, as we all cheered each other on and exchanged thoughts about our literary adventures.\",\"user\",[63]],[\"s39\",\"d5\",107,396,\"User: On a positive note, I started a regular volunteering schedule at the local library. It's been a great way to engage with the community and help out with outreach programs. Every week, I look forward to connecting with people of all ages who share a passion for reading and learning. \",\"user\",[147]],[\"s40\",\"d5\",396,630,\"There’s something special about watching children’s faces light up when they discover a new book or hear a story being read aloud. It’s rewarding to think that I’m playing a small part in fostering a love for literacy in my community.\",\"user\",[147]],[\"s47\",\"d6\",107,342,\"User: I thought being part of a community-based buying group would be a great way to connect with others who share similar interests and values, especially since it promised the potential for bulk discounts on items we frequently use. \",\"user\",[140]],[\"s48\",\"d6\",342,721,\"However, after attending a few meetings, I realized that the dynamics were quite different from what I had imagined, lacking the vibrant exchanges and enthusiastic interactions that I had hoped for. I was particularly looking forward to discussing various products and hearing diverse opinions, as I believed this would enrich my shopping experience and decision-making process. \",\"user\",[140]],[\"s49\",\"d6\",721,1007,\"Instead, the conversations felt a bit mundane and not as engaging as I had anticipated, making me question the value of my membership. As I sat there, I couldn't help but think that perhaps my expectations had been set too high or that this particular group wasn't the right fit for me.\",\"user\",[140]],[\"s57\",\"d7\",105,438,\"User: In fact, I curated a list of must-read books for a community newsletter. It was gratifying to craft something that I hope could inspire and encourage readers all around me. Diving into the world of literature and selecting titles that resonate with different audiences is a unique challenge, but one that is deeply fulfilling. \",\"user\",[19]],[\"s58\",\"d7\",438,707,\"Each book carries its own unique message and has the potential to change perspectives, and I find joy in sharing those insights with others. It provides me a sense of connection with my community, knowing that I might influence someone’s reading journey for the better.\",\"user\",[19]],[\"s77\",\"d8\",105,455,\"User: Volunteering at a library where I helped organize book recommendations for patrons was an incredibly rewarding experience that deepened my appreciation for literature. There is something profoundly satisfying about assisting others in finding the right book that resonates with them, enhancing their reading journey through curated selections. \",\"user\",[21]],[\"s78\",\"d8\",455,740,\"Each book has its unique charm and potential to transport readers to another world or teach them something new, and being part of that process felt meaningful. It was also a joy to interact with patrons from various backgrounds, each with their unique stories and reading preferences. \",\"user\",[21]],[\"s79\",\"d8\",740,859,\"Knowing that my efforts contributed to fostering a community devoted to reading made every moment spent there worth it.\",\"user\",[21]],[\"s95\",\"d9\",103,424,\"User: For starters, I joined a local book club focused on contemporary fiction. This decision came after realizing how much I missed discussing books with others, especially after spending so much time reading alone. The club has opened my eyes to new authors and perspectives that I might never have explored on my own. \",\"user\",[3]],[\"s96\",\"d9\",424,769,\"Connecting with others who share similar interests in narrative styles and themes has also enriched my understanding of contemporary issues reflected in literature. I've found myself excitedly anticipating each meeting, as they not only discuss the stories themselves, but also the emotional and cultural contexts that inform these modern works.\",\"user\",[3]],[\"s104\",\"d10\",107,450,\"User: On a creative note, I formed a partnership with local artists to create unique book-themed merchandise for upcoming events. Working together has opened up an entirely new world of possibilities for our designs. It's fascinating to see how their individual styles are being blended with literary themes to create something truly special. \",\"user\",[162]],[\"s105\",\"d10\",450,779,\"I'm particularly thrilled about the prospect of showcasing these items at our future events, as I believe they will resonate deeply with book lovers and attendees alike. The whole process has invigorated my enthusiasm for both reading and community engagement, making every brainstorming session feel like a delightful adventure.\",\"user\",[162]],[\"s112\",\"d11\",103,467,\"User: I've recently explored my passion for books more deeply this year. It has been a transformative journey as I have immersed myself in various genres that pique my interest, ranging from classic literature to contemporary novels. I've found that reading not only enriches my imagination but also enhances my understanding of diverse cultures and perspectives. \",\"user\",[1]],[\"s113\",\"d11\",467,749,\"With each book I pick up, I discover new worlds that broaden my horizons and challenge my viewpoints. This newfound engagement with literature has ignited a desire to share my thoughts and interpretations with others, perhaps leading to discussions or even book clubs in the future.\",\"user\",[1]],[\"s120\",\"d12\",103,434,\"User: Just last month I attended a national literature festival featuring various authors. The experience was truly inspiring, as I was able to engage in meaningful conversations with writers whose work I deeply admire. It was also fascinating to see the different approaches to storytelling that each author brought to the table. \",\"user\",[7]],[\"s121\",\"d12\",434,697,\"The atmosphere was electric, filled with the buzz of literary enthusiasts, and I felt a sense of belonging amidst people who shared my passion for literature. I left the festival with a renewed sense of purpose and a desire to dive deeper into the world of books.\",\"user\",[7]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"lifetime\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"public_output_question\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\",\"public_options\":[\"It seems like you're questioning whether the time commitment aligns with your other responsibilities. Balancing event planning with personal activities can be challenging. It might be worthwhile to evaluate if this is the right time to continue, or if easing back could give you more freedom. What are your thoughts on adjusting your involvement?\",\"It appears you're pondering your passion for event planning in your community. Community engagement is valuable, but it's also important to feel motivated and interested in what you're doing. Maybe explore different roles or activities that might reignite your enthusiasm. How does that sound to you?\",\"It sounds like you might be feeling a bit overwhelmed or finding the process less enjoyable than before. If the structured planning is becoming tedious, perhaps focusing on more spontaneous or informal engagement within the community could be a refreshing change. Consider activities that require less meticulous planning and more personal interaction. How do you feel about trying something like that?\",\"It sounds like you're in a period of reflection about what you enjoy most. Community events can be rewarding and stressful at the same time. Perhaps exploring other interests or roles can provide a sense of fulfillment without the pressure. Do you think trying out different activities might help you decide?\"],\"terminal_express